The transpose of a matrix interchanges its rows and columns; this is illustrated below:

$$
\left[ \begin{array}{l l l l} A 1 1 & A 1 2 & A 1 3 & A 1 4 \\ A 2 1 & A 2 2 & A 2 3 & A 2 4 \\ A 3 1 & A 3 2 & A 3 3 & A 3 4 \\ A 4 1 & A 4 2 & A 4 3 & A 4 4 \end{array} \right] \Rightarrow \left[ \begin{array}{l l l l} A 1 1 & A 2 1 & A 3 1 & A 4 1 \\ A 1 2 & A 2 2 & A 3 2 & A 4 2 \\ A 1 3 & A 2 3 & A 3 3 & A 4 3 \\ A 1 4 & A 2 4 & A 3 4 & A 4 4 \end{array} \right]
$$

Here is a simple C loop to show the transpose:

```c

for (i = 0; i < 3; i++) {

    for (j = 0; j < 3; j++) {

        output[j][i] = input[i][j];

    }

}

```

